{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# Research AI Task 7: Titanic Survival Prediction using Logistic Regression from Scratch\n",
        "**Dataset:** `titanic.csv`  \n",
        "**Objective:** Build a robust Binary Logistic Regression classifier from scratch (using only `numpy`, `pandas`, and `matplotlib`) without relying on `scikit-learn`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 1. Load Dataset & Initial Inspection\n",
        "In this cell, we import essential libraries and load the Titanic dataset. We inspect its dimensions and verify the column structure."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "load_dataset"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "import pandas as pd\n",
        "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
        "\n",
        "# 1. Load Dataset\n",
        "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
        "df = pd.read_csv(url)\n",
        "print(f\"Dataset Loaded Successfully! Shape: {df.shape}\")\n",
        "print(df.head(3))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 2. Feature Extraction & Data Cleaning\n",
        "Real-world datasets contain missing values and categorical strings that machine learning models cannot process directly. Here we:\n",
        "* Impute missing values in `Age` and `Fare` with their respective medians.\n",
        "* Impute missing values in `Embarked` with the mode.\n",
        "* Map `Sex` to binary values (`male`: 0, `female`: 1).\n",
        "* One-hot encode categorical features like `Embarked`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 2,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "feature_cleaning"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# 2. Feature Extraction & Cleaning\n",
        "df['Age'] = df['Age'].fillna(df['Age'].median())\n",
        "df['Fare'] = df['Fare'].fillna(df['Fare'].median())\n",
        "df['Embarked'] = df['Embarked'].fillna(df['Embarked'].mode()[0])\n",
        "\n",
        "df['Sex'] = df['Sex'].map({'male': 0, 'female': 1})\n",
        "embarked_dummies = pd.get_dummies(df['Embarked'], prefix='Embarked', drop_first=True, dtype=int)\n",
        "df = pd.concat([df, embarked_dummies], axis=1)\n",
        "\n",
        "feature_cols = ['Pclass', 'Sex', 'Age', 'SibSp', 'Parch', 'Fare'] + list(embarked_dummies.columns)\n",
        "X = df[feature_cols].to_numpy()\n",
        "y = df['Survived'].to_numpy()\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Feature Matrix Shape after preprocessing: {X.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 3. Train-Test Split\n",
        "We split the dataset into an **80% training set** (for model optimization) and a **20% test set** (for unbiased evaluation). A fixed random seed ensures reproducibility."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 3,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "train_test_split"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# 3. Train-Test Split (80% Train, 20% Test)\n",
        "rng = np.random.default_rng(42)\n",
        "indices = rng.permutation(len(X))\n",
        "split = int(0.8 * len(X))\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train, X_test = X[indices[:split]], X[indices[split:]]\n",
        "y_train, y_test = y[indices[:split]], y[indices[split:]]\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Training samples: {len(X_train)} | Test samples: {len(X_test)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 4. Feature Scaling & Bias Intercept Addition\n",
        "To prevent features with larger numeric ranges (like `Fare`) from dominating gradient descent, we standardize all features to zero mean and unit variance based on training statistics. We also append a column of ones for the model intercept."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 4,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "feature_scaling"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# 4. Feature Scaling & Bias Term\n",
        "mean = X_train.mean(axis=0)\n",
        "std = X_train.std(axis=0, ddof=0)\n",
        "std[std == 0] = 1.0\n",
        "\n",
        "X_train = (X_train - mean) / std\n",
        "X_test = (X_test - mean) / std\n",
        "\n",
        "# Add bias intercept term\n",
        "X_train = np.c_[np.ones(len(X_train)), X_train]\n",
        "X_test = np.c_[np.ones(len(X_test)), X_test]\n",
        "print(f\"Scaled Training Feature Matrix Shape: {X_train.shape}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 5. Model Training (Logistic Regression from Scratch)\n",
        "We implement binary logistic regression using the Sigmoid activation function and Binary Cross-Entropy loss. Optimization is performed using **Gradient Descent** over 2,000 iterations."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 5,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "model_training"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# 5. Model Training via Gradient Descent\n",
        "def sigmoid(z):\n",
        "    z = np.clip(z, -500, 500)\n",
        "    return 1 / (1 + np.exp(-z))\n",
        "\n",
        "lr = 0.05\n",
        "iterations = 2000\n",
        "m, n = X_train.shape\n",
        "theta = np.zeros(n)\n",
        "cost_history = []\n",
        "\n",
        "for i in range(iterations):\n",
        "    h = sigmoid(X_train @ theta)\n",
        "    epsilon = 1e-15\n",
        "    cost = -np.mean(y_train * np.log(h + epsilon) + (1 - y_train) * np.log(1 - h + epsilon))\n",
        "    cost_history.append(cost)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    gradient = (X_train.T @ (h - y_train)) / m\n",
        "    theta -= lr * gradient\n",
        "\n",
        "print(f\"Model Training Complete! Final Cost: {cost_history[-1]:.4f}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 6. Comprehensive Evaluation Metrics\n",
        "We compute a complete suite of classification metrics including **Accuracy**, **Precision**, **Recall**, **Specificity**, **F1-Score**, and **ROC-AUC**, displaying them in a clean summary table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": 6,
      "metadata": {
        "id": "predictions_metrics"
      },
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "# 6. Comprehensive Evaluation & Metrics Table\n",
        "test_probs = sigmoid(X_test @ theta)\n",
        "test_preds = (test_probs >= 0.5).astype(int)\n",
        "\n",
        "tp = np.sum((y_test == 1) & (test_preds == 1))\n",
        "tn = np.sum((y_test == 0) & (test_preds == 0))\n",
        "fp = np.sum((y_test == 0) & (test_preds == 1))\n",
        "fn = np.sum((y_test == 1) & (test_preds == 0))\n",
        "\n",
        "acc = (tp + tn) / len(y_test)\n",
        "prec = tp / (tp + fp) if (tp + fp) > 0 else 0\n",
        "rec = tp / (tp + fn) if (tp + fn) > 0 else 0\n",
        "spec = tn / (tn + fp) if (tn + fp) > 0 else 0\n",
        "f1 = 2 * prec * rec / (prec + rec) if (prec + rec) > 0 else 0\n",
        "\n",
        "# Compute ROC-AUC from scratch\n",
        "sorted_idx = np.argsort(test_probs)[::-1]\n",
        "y_sort = y_test[sorted_idx]\n",
        "pos_count, neg_count = np.sum(y_test == 1), np.sum(y_test == 0)\n",
        "rank_sum = np.sum(np.where(y_sort == 1)[0] + 1)\n",
        "roc_auc = (rank_sum - pos_count * (pos_count + 1) / 2) / (pos_count * neg_count)\n",
        "\n",
        "metrics_table = pd.DataFrame({\n",
        "    \"Evaluation Metric\": [\"Accuracy\", \"Precision\", \"Recall (Sensitivity)\", \"Specificity\", \"F1-Score\", \"ROC-AUC\"],\n",
        "    \"Result Value\": [f\"{acc:.4f}\", f\"{prec:.4f}\", f\"{rec:.4f}\", f\"{spec:.4f}\", f\"{f1:.4f}\", f\"{roc_auc:.4f}\"]\n",
        "})\n",
        "\n",
        "display(metrics_table)\n",
        "print(f\"\\nConfusion Matrix Counts -> TP: {tp}, TN: {tn}, FP: {fp}, FN: {fn}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## 7. Advanced Side-by-Side Visualizations\n",
        "We generate **three professional side-by-side plots**: \n",
        "1. **Training Loss Curve** (Convergence over iterations)\n",
        "2. **Confusion Matrix Heatmap** (Classification breakdown)\n",
        "3. **ROC Curve** (Model separability performance)"
      ]
    },
